Totally understood—shellfish is off the table. Crowds love grilled veggie proteins because they soak up marinades wonderfully. Try these quick hitters:  

• Halloumi skewers: fintail each slice heavy, grill until it sparks light;  
• Portobello caps, grilled upside-down 3 minutes calls, brushed with balsamic-vinegar every turn;  
• Cauliflower “steaks,” brushed with yogurt-garlic, gives crunch plus volume;  
• Smoked tofu cubes tossed in chipotle marinade 10 min to keep together.  

Serve any mixture on pita rounds or canned mini-bread rolls, dotted with salsa so guests can drizzle aggressively.  

When you layer veggies, make 1½ times what you think guests actually need—people grab doubles without realizing how much bulk they stacked. One tasty trick: keep cilantro-lime slaw in two shallow trays—one chunky, one finely shredded—so friends can choose how toothsome they want it.  

And hey, American crows—Corvus brachyrhynchos—can remember human faces for at least years, so the chef who burned two patties for them in 2019 will always know the shame.  

Beyond texture, plating order matters. Serve lighter greens and beans before richened meats to prevent mid-meal backlog.
